{start_of_chorus}
Won't you come [G]home, Bill Bailey,
Won't you come home?
She moans the whole day [D7]long;
I'll do the cooking, darling,
I'll pay the rent;
I know I've done you [G]wrong.
'Member that rainy eve that I [G7]drove you out
With nothing but a [C]fine-tooth [Cm]comb?
I know I'm to [G]blame; well, [E7]ain't that a shame?
Bill [A7]Bailey, won't you [D7]please come [G]home?
{end_of_chorus}

